<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ciona intestinalis Turing wavelength at 51 µm (5.056e-05 m), Holocene 0 Ma — MorphoEval overall 82.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg activator-inhibitor kinetics on a periodic 4-wavelength patch, with gamma set so lambda_c = 5.056e-05 m (tier label 51 µm, log10 = -4.296, tier 4_cellular_10um, detail). Age 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1. Critical-mode log-amplitude Pearson r = 0.9994 on the linear window. Numerical radial-FFT wavelength 50.05 µm against the 50.56 µm pin. Equal-diffusion amplitude ratio 1.98e-5 and gamma=0 ratio 2.80e-4, against a Turing ratio 2.95. YPM IZ 082346 (CC0) body length 34.0 mm on the 10 mm bar; adult pigment spacing 873 µm, which is not the detail-tier wavelength. The image-fitness JSON for the loop is not assembled yet. Overall 82.2/100 (faithfulness 81.1, reproducibility 84.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 25e28a4514fe1c49bc401d10321c28551fd40114; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, pillow, matplotlib. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml on this runner.. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/ciona_intestinalis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 25e28a4514fe1c49bc401d10321c28551fd40114, image/png, 277777 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 cc584dd710e4101b0d3ba109c77c4f2a8b5d0881f3f440ea85b9160379bea4c6 (sha256 cc584dd710e4101b0d3ba109c77c4f2a8b5d0881f3f440ea85b9160379bea4c6), spec_fingerprint cc8077f6425fa5fa7578c008956e84c51354ee6ba24c3850292df68d0c32e0f9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cc8077f6425fa5fa7578c008956e84c51354ee6ba24c3850292df68d0c32e0f9; artifact_sha256: cc584dd710e4101b0d3ba109c77c4f2a8b5d0881f3f440ea85b9160379bea4c6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ciona_intestinalis_turing_wavelength_s0/Ciona_intestinalis_YPM_IZ_082346.jpg=bacc05b7298b188c..., datasets/ciona_intestinalis_turing_wavelength_s0/ciona_intestinalis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=ba8af50f6e980b7c..., datasets/ciona_intestinalis_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=6b138fabe89be7a0...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetic scheme used here. | Ciona pigment cells are a neural-crest-like lineage (Abitua et al. 2012). Jeffery et al. (2004) showed migratory pigment cells in a urochordate. The larval ocellus and otolith sit in the sensory vesicle (Hudson 2016; Kourakis et al. 2021; Hotta et al. 2007).; reconstructed_in_script: gamma, Du and Dv are chosen so the analytical lambda_c equals the slot pin 5.056e-05 m. They are not a regression onto a Ciona dose-response curve. | The growth GIF paints the activator inside the segmented YPM body. Computer-vision similarity to that photograph is a silhouette-and-texture score, not a claim that the adult tunic stripes at 51 µm.; transfer_boundary: Chronoseries length is 1, so there is no temporal predecessor. The scale sandwich is melanosome (1 µm) < detail patch (4 × 51 µm) < adult body on the 10 mm bar. | Adult red-channel spacing on this photograph is 873 µm. That number must not be quoted as a measurement of k_c.; does_not_claim: Does not claim u and v are identified Ciona morphogens. | Does not claim Brunetti et al. (2015) type A versus type B was resolved from this photograph. | Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present on this runner.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.1]: Record adult spacing versus the 51 µm pin as a scale-transfer control with value != reference.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.3]: Assemble the loop image-fitness JSON from the measured CV similarity and the pass-2 rubric subscores.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Write morphoeval/runs/2026-10-27-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-loop-image-fitness.json with image_fitness = 0.55*CV + 0.30*specimen-match + 0.15*morphometric-validation, n_frames, resolution, and non-circular specimen metrics (value != reference).'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Keep the dispersion panel zoomed on the unstable band so sigma(k_c) > 0 is visible, and quote the equal-diffusion amplitude ratio in scientific notation rather than as 0.00.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Publish the adult pigment spacing (about 873 µm) next to the 50.56 µm pin as an explicit scale-transfer control in the pass-2 measurements sidecar.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.22e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ciona intestinalis Turing wavelength at 51 µm (5.056e-05 m), Holocene 0 Ma — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
